<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 12 July, from 1191 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1191 CE <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Acre surrenders to the armies of the Third Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of almost two years, the garrison of Acre surrendered to Richard I and Philip II. The port became the crusaders' main base and later capital of the Kingdom of Jerusalem.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1543 CE <span class="tih-ago">483 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII marries Catherine Parr, his sixth wife</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VIII married the twice-widowed Catherine Parr at Hampton Court. She outlived him, helped reconcile the king with his daughters and became the first English queen to publish a book in her own name.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1691 CE <span class="tih-ago">335 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Williamite army wins the Battle of Aughrim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William III's forces under Godert de Ginkel defeated the Jacobite army at Aughrim in County Galway (12 July Old Style). The bloodiest battle in Irish history effectively decided the Williamite war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1862 CE <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln signs the act creating the Army Medal of Honor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Lincoln signed a resolution authorising the Medal of Honor for army soldiers who distinguished themselves by gallantry. It remains the highest US military decoration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet and German tanks clash at Prokhorovka</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet tank armies counter-attacked the SS Panzer Corps at Prokhorovka, one of the largest tank battles in history. The Soviets lost heavily, but the German offensive at Kursk was halted.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1997 CE <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malala Yousafzai is born in Pakistan's Swat Valley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malala Yousafzai was born in Mingora. Shot by the Taliban in 2012 for campaigning for girls' education, she survived and in 2014 became the youngest Nobel Peace Prize laureate.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
